      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "The matrix transformation never runs \u2014 the conversion got there first",
      "description": "**Identical to the chord above, and that is the finding.**\n\nSame query and the same **Convert field type** + **Grouping to matrix** transformations as the table on the left \u2014 yet this panel draws the six edge-per-field ribbons rather than a matrix.\n\nA panel-registered conversion is a pipeline **prefix**: `legacyToWide` runs *before* the user's transformations, so by the time `groupingToMatrix` runs there is no `source`, `target` or `mainstat` column left to group by and it returns its input unchanged. Measured \u2014 this panel's tooltips are identical to the chord above, `a \u2192 b 10` through `c \u2192 b 60`.\n\nTwo consequences worth knowing:\n\n- **A user transformation that consumes the row format is unreachable on this panel.** That is the price of the prefix, and the prefix is what makes every mark an override target.\n- Nothing is lost *today*: the matrix **interpretation** \u2014 a column is a node, a cell is an edge \u2014 is specified but unimplemented. `frameToGraphWide` returns `null` for a matrix frame (measured), and the matrix interpretation was subsequently rejected outright. See [data-plane/graph-matrix.md](../../../data-plane/graph-matrix.md), which records why the matrix interpretation was rejected.",
